# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Deploy configs — not needed inside the image
deploy/
scripts/

# PHASE 106A — narrow re-include for the journal importer.
#
# `scripts/` above stays a blanket exclusion: no other image gets any of it.
# This exception admits ONLY scripts/journal into the build CONTEXT, which is
# what the `journal-importer` stage COPYies. Nothing else changes — the runner
# and migrator stages have no COPY of `scripts/`, so re-including these files
# cannot put them in the web or migration images.
#
# Docker (unlike git) descends into an excluded directory when any `!` exception
# exists, and the LAST matching pattern wins. So ordering matters twice over:
# this exception must come AFTER `scripts/` to take effect, and BEFORE the
# `**/__tests__/` and `**/*.test.ts` rules below so those still strip the
# importer's own test files back out. Both are proven mechanically by
# scripts/__tests__/phase106a-journal-import-path.test.ts and by the image
# audit in the Phase 106A runbook.
!scripts/journal

# Test files
**/__tests__/
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
vitest.config.*

# Docs
DEPLOYMENT.md
*.md

# Backups
backups/
*.sql
*.sql.gz
